WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.039
Part twelve: tax rules. Every slab, rebate, cap and due date the portal works with, in one place - read-only for everyone but the portal owner. Here is the owner.

2
00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:23.980
Not checked for thirty days: the department may have published something since. A reminder - never a call made by itself.

3
00:00:24.593 --> 00:00:41.103
Pick the year - the next one, or this year again - and an A I: Gemini or OpenAI, both searching the web, with the owner's own key. For this film the answer was saved beforehand, and made up: no A I is called.

4
00:00:41.718 --> 00:00:47.288
Four figures changed, thirty-four the same, and three not announced yet.

5
00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:59.390
Side by side, this year's and the next: the new regime's slabs, the standard deduction, the 80 C cap and the due date - each change marked, with its source.

6
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.259
Only the changes.

7
00:01:02.875 --> 00:01:08.155
Surcharge is not announced yet: it stays as it is until it is.

8
00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:18.689
A change that is not a figure - a new fee - is listed to be built, never guessed into a rule. And the pages it read, here made up.

9
00:01:19.297 --> 00:01:30.477
Tick what is right and apply. The figures go into the rules through the same builder as every chip - with History - and last year's slabs stay for past years.

10
00:01:31.078 --> 00:01:39.118
The new year is now live: every return on the portal - a CA firm's or your own - works with its figures.

11
00:01:39.718 --> 00:01:45.858
And the rule book: every rule SimplyFile works by, written out in one place.

12
00:01:46.468 --> 00:01:59.568
Your own return from your documents, a firm's families and consultants, and the year's rules kept up to date - all SimplyFile's own rules, kept as chips. Thank you for watching.
